what REDS %765, OPEN and unclaimed, whose audit half names a population nothing reads: 111 counted version strings across 42 record families stand in authored Rye, and the molt of the 41 unmoved families wants Keaton's word. The agent-doable half is the reading. Measured this lap over git history, the population GROWS -- 20 families on 20260801, 36 on 20260901, 39 today -- so counted headers keep being written in the retired style while the molt waits. A ratchet holding it from growing costs no stored byte and makes the next arrival visible on the lap it lands. The crux is the DISCRIMINATOR rather than the grep: a record version is a string reaching stored bytes as a format or header field -- written by append_kv with a format key, compared against a parsed format or header, or declared as a *_format or format_tag constant -- and the naive pattern admits three strings that are no version at all (a test file's CONTENT in mantra/recall_two_way_sync.rye, a witness plaintext in mand/mand_ring1_witness.rye, a fixture signature value in mantra/src/receipt_offer_witness.rye). So the row's own 111 across 42 is a grep's number and this reading answers it classified. Report chronological beside counted, since mantra-weave-20260916.101910 is the one family moved and the meter must show a molt when it happens. Ratchet, never a wall: every counted header opens a store this tree already wrote, and accrete-never-break keeps them forever. No record header moved, no peer file touched.
