what The root-finder ratchet is red on every ship right now -- finders_bare_unrunnable reads 191 against a ceiling of 189 -- for two finders BORN in 32 upstream commits that no ship chose and this one cannot sweep. My own last lap named the cause on the card: a ratchet that only falls, over a population every lane ADDS to, is a wall with a delay, and the no-slack reasoning that is right for a fixed population inverts for a growing one. Growth reads roughly two an hour of fleet time, each a hand copying one of the 189 examples the tree ships. The cure is to gate the GROWTH rather than the total. Pin the seating population as a tracked baseline roster of PATHS, then split the one number in two: finders_bare_new, a bare finder in a file absent from the roster, GATED at zero, since a file born today is born in somebody's current lane and is repairable on the lap it lands; and finders_bare_legacy, the roster's own files, held under a ceiling that only falls, which is now a ratchet over a FIXED population where no-slack is right again. Keying the roster by PATH while the legacy ceiling counts SITES is the composition that leaves no hole: a new file reds the growth gate, and a new finder added to a roster file raises the site count past the falling ceiling. Name the one false red this shape can make -- a lawful rename of a roster file -- and its repair, one roster row, which is the same cost as the elder ceiling edit and visible rather than silent. Prove both readings from both sides in the existing pen, with a mutation that empties the roster and must bite. No finder swept, no peer file touched.
claim patchouli-build-lock-swept-by-round-open
seat patchouli
stamp 20260917.061842
